@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# v42 — Screenshot sweep and cursor recovery
+
+Fast map sweep now captures a ready gameplay view, checks its owned screenshot in
+a background worker and continues navigating. Empty views avoid the full 1.2s
+inspection dwell. If the saved image contains a gem candidate, the main patrol
+releases any map drag, returns to that exact saved camera view and confirms the
+gem again on fresh frames before clicking. Old screenshot coordinates are never
+clicked after navigation. The original screenshot, spotted time and camera
+location stay attached to one history/counter entry after confirmation.
+
+Only one screenshot can be in flight. The last screenshot is resolved before a
+pass can finish. An uncertain/loading scene uses normal temporal inspection;
+a candidate that disappears on return is not counted or clicked. The unfinished
+next route location remains unchecked and is resumed. F10 discards pending work,
+releases input and never restarts. Gem Spy retains its observation timing.
+
+Fast map sweep is on by default in Sniper settings. Turning it off restores fixed
+loading waits and full multi-frame inspection on every view. The v41 UI handoff
+that ignored the saved speed preference is corrected. Custom loading delays are
+honored. A quick sweep samples one ready screenshot per view; turn it off for the
+longer observation window when gems render late. Positive candidates still need
+the normal multi-frame/0.8s confirmation after return. Detector thresholds and
+map/route assets are unchanged.
+
+The reported mouse-position stop now has bounded recovery. Before mouse-down,
+a transient mismatch gets up to two reposition retries at 15ms intervals; an
+exact, eligible target is still required. A mismatch while held releases input
+and retries the unfinished route location from fresh map recognition, at most
+twice per progress checkpoint. Persistent errors, changed window geometry, lost
+focus, obstruction and F10 still stop. Recovery after an already-recorded find
+never re-records it. Normal pointer operations have no added wait.
+
+The 20-second collection wait, Emerald Corner return, daily obtained choices,
+Endless mode, histories, heatmaps, compact UI and MuMu mouse backend remain.
+Keep MuMu visible, uncovered and focused. No ADB is used. Exit the old app,
+extract the whole package and run LoongLens.exe; LocalAppData is retained.
+
+Validation includes delayed detection while a map is open or a held pan is in
+progress, last-view draining, cancellation, lost candidates, original evidence,
+worker errors, pointer drift/retries/limits and real Windows delivered input.
+Full-route comparisons with v37 and v41 use simulated input and already-rendered
+scenes; they do not measure live MuMu speed or actual game loading behavior.
